<!-- The D.R.I. complaint's Word styles: the cross-engine recipe (tools/fb/src/docxxengine.rs) in the face of the typst
     template ({font}, Times New Roman) at 12 pt (size 24 half points; LR Cv 5(a)(3): at least 12-point type); Body
     Text in exact 27.6 pt line boxes (typst pitch-double: LR Cv 5(a)(3) double spacing, Word's "double" for 12 pt
     Times, RID-FORM-009) with a half-inch first-line indent, and the headings in them; the caption, signature and
     footer lines in 13.8 pt boxes (typst pitch-single); letter page with 1-inch margins and the page number at the
     bottom center (LR Cv 5(a)(3)), its line 36.6 pt above the page foot (732 twips: where typst sets it,
     footer-descent 30 %). One style replaced: Heading 1 without the recipe's capitals (typst sets the
     headings as written). docx/rid-complaint.lua writes every paragraph's own spacing. Twips: 20 x pt. -->
<reference xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" base="xengine" size="24" body="552" single="276" indent="720" heading="552" heading-before="0" heading-after="0" footer="732">
